  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#45126\", \"PowerToys#39704\", \"PowerToys#41229\"], \"answer\": \"This is a known limitation, not a new bug. Windows does not deliver keystrokes from an elevated (admin) window to a low-level keyboard hook running at a lower privilege level. PowerToys itself being elevated is not enough: the Command Palette process is started separately and may not be elevated, which you can check in Task Manager. In the past tickets, the hotkey worked once Command Palette was quit and restarted as administrator, and it works fine when a non-elevated window has focus. Be aware that running Command Palette elevated makes every app launched from it elevated too, so many users do not want that. Also confirm that 'Use low-level keyboard hook' is actually enabled. The team has added a note in the Command Palette activation shortcut settings that explains this limitation.\"}",
